From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:29:11 -0400
Subject: fix: cut unwired helpers and close the open holes

The approved cuts leave the product: throwaway Spaces, copy-tab,
the clipboard fence, host-route helper, split restore, the orphan
window model, blank-window in-memory jars, folder insert-between,
folders moving as units, the sidebar v2 file, scheduled backups
and backup restore, Chromium's command-bar registry, the Mac Tab
menu's group rows, little-window and popup idle close, and
automatic bookmarks-to-pins.

Quit restores nested folders in order with their ids. The command
bar runs the highlighted row, stays on the active Space while Hide
Other Spaces is on, and Command-L navigates the current tab. The
horizontal strip uses the same Space, pin and folder model. Welcome
and settings can import bookmarks, history and passwords from a
Chromium-family profile. Settings watches the Space registry, and
screenshots do not keep a raw profile pointer across the capture.

Why: these were the holes the owner already approved, and the specs
still described behaviour the product did not have.
Removable when: the series is rebased onto a Chromium that has
equivalent behaviour upstream.
